            <div xml:id="d881">

                <pb facs="0936" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/992: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-03T13:00:00-05:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                                1920—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 4—1:55
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>46. …</p>
                <p>My July 28, 4 p.m. The President has vetoed the act referred to on the advice of
                    the junta of notables apparently with pressure of Great Britain. Congress has
                    referred it to a special committee and may pass it over the veto.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
